{"text": "To get the target value of 24 using the numbers [6, 7, 9, 9] exactly once with the operations +, -, *, /, here's one way to do it:", "start": 0, "end": 130, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(7 - (9/9)) × 6 = (7 - 1) × 6 = 6 × 6 = 36", "start": 132, "end": 174, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Oops, that's not 24.", "start": 175, "end": 195, "label": "correction"}
{"text": "Let's try another approach:", "start": 196, "end": 223, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "9 × (9 - 7) + 6 = 9 × 2 + 6 = 18 + 6 = 24", "start": 225, "end": 266, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So, the solution is:", "start": 268, "end": 288, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 × (9 - 7) + 6 = 24", "start": 290, "end": 310, "label": "inform"}
